Subject: [REVIEW 02/16] Qualcomm USB4 clocks, reset errors and USB power domain retention

Add Glymur router clock/mux operations, propagate reset errors, and expose the DP input link clock. Keep the ten Glymur USB controller and PHY power domains in retention (PWRSTS_RET_ON), as X1E and SC8280XP do: with them allowed to switch off, the front-port controller faulted and died after resume. The USB4 router domains are unchanged. Review register ownership, bounded polling and error unwinding.

Dependencies: Base prerequisites. Used by patches 05, 07, 11 and 16.

Source attribution: Local Surface integration; provenance/usb4/05-glymur-p2rr2p-mux.diff, 06-glymur-rx-mux.diff and 20-clk-qcom-reset-propagate-errors.patch; remaining changes, including the retention change from Surface candidate 1.90, are recorded in provenance/derivation.json.

This is a review grouping of preserved source, not a new authorship claim or
an independently build-validated upstream commit. Original attribution remains
in the referenced provenance files. No new Signed-off-by trailers are added.

